WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:02.131
- We're in Mexico and we
had to stop by Starbucks

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:05.077
because there are three
cool drinks that we found.

00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:05.910
And we're gonna try it.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.618
(wind whipping)
(hinge squeaks)

00:00:07.618 --> 00:00:09.148
(techno music)

00:00:09.148 --> 00:00:12.413
- My go to drink for Starbucks
is usually an iced chai.

00:00:12.413 --> 00:00:13.308
- Iced vanilla latte.

00:00:13.308 --> 00:00:16.604
- Just a regular latte.
- I like espresso Frappuccino.

00:00:16.604 --> 00:00:19.452
- Recently I've just been
having a lot of cold brew.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.510
So this is going to be interesting

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.536
how different.
- Yeah.

00:00:21.536 --> 00:00:23.504
- And sugary (laughs) it is.
- Oh yeah.

00:00:23.504 --> 00:00:24.597
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.597 --> 00:00:26.059
- So this is Cajeta Frappuccino.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:26.892
- Excellent.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.359
- I never get the super sugary drinks.

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:30.988
Just looking at this is a little bit

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:32.036
like wow.
- Yeah.

00:00:32.036 --> 00:00:32.937
- That's a lot.

00:00:32.937 --> 00:00:35.051
- It has some chocolaty chunks?

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:39.290
- Yeah chocolaty chunks
and chocolate dust.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.123
Oh.

00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:43.132
- Wow.
- It's intense.

00:00:43.132 --> 00:00:44.215
- It's really good.

00:00:44.215 --> 00:00:46.588
- It's definitely not something
I would order on my own.

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:48.753
More than a couple sips
of that is just too much.

00:00:48.753 --> 00:00:51.783
- Definitely a bigger punch
then just like a caramel frap.

00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:52.752
- I like it, wow.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.169
- I would get a sugar high from this.

00:00:54.169 --> 00:00:56.624
- The coffee was stronger than I expected.

00:00:56.624 --> 00:00:57.457
- I would get this.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.748
(wind whips)

00:00:58.748 --> 00:01:00.827
- I've never had Mexican
hot chocolate before.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.083
- [Juan] Oh, you're in for a treat.

00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:05.138
- I always order hot
chocolates from Starbucks

00:01:05.138 --> 00:01:06.804
so I'm pretty excited for this one.

00:01:06.804 --> 00:01:08.557
- So what's the difference
between hot chocolate

00:01:08.557 --> 00:01:10.582
in the US and Mexican hot chocolate?

00:01:10.582 --> 00:01:13.161
- There's a very specific
brand called Chocolate Abuelita

00:01:13.161 --> 00:01:14.644
and it's just a little bar of chocolate

00:01:14.644 --> 00:01:17.057
that you put in a pot and
then there's a little tool

00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:17.890
that you use.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.441
It makes it nice and frothy.

00:01:20.441 --> 00:01:21.289
- Whoa.

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:23.967
Oh this is great.
- Are you into it?

00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:25.575
- I feel like I should
be wrapped in a blanket

00:01:25.575 --> 00:01:26.677
in front of a fire.
(laughs)

00:01:26.677 --> 00:01:27.942
- It smells very heartwarming.

00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:29.642
- It is like Christmas day.

00:01:29.642 --> 00:01:31.599
- There's something besides the cinnamon.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:33.829
- Nutmeg kind of like feel.

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:35.531
- I would always have
this during Christmas.

00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:37.786
- Yeah I can see it as a
Christmas drink, totally.

00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:40.623
(wind whips)
- This is a Mango Frap.

00:01:40.623 --> 00:01:42.110
It doesn't smell like mango.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.449
- I'm nervous about this one.

00:01:43.449 --> 00:01:44.687
- It looks like pumpkin.

00:01:44.687 --> 00:01:47.318
- This will be interesting.

00:01:47.318 --> 00:01:48.187
- That's refreshing.

00:01:48.187 --> 00:01:49.354
- That's actually really good.

00:01:49.354 --> 00:01:50.625
- That's sweet.

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:52.583
- Not really a fan of
sour mangoes in general.

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:54.596
- I love sour stuff so that's
probably why I like it.

00:01:54.596 --> 00:01:57.507
- I think this is the
equivalent of a berry refresher

00:01:57.507 --> 00:01:58.340
at Starbucks.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.704
Definitely towards the Mexican flavor.

00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:02.283
- Mexican Starbucks.

00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:04.480
(bell rings)
This was by far my favorite.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.538
(wind whips)
- I would have to say the

00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:06.686
(bell rings)
hot chocolate was my favorite.

00:02:06.686 --> 00:02:07.740
(wind whips)
- So nostalgic

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.591
(bell rings)
to holiday cheer.

00:02:09.591 --> 00:02:10.424
(wind whips)
- This impressed me

00:02:10.424 --> 00:02:11.662
(bell rings)
because it was fresher,

00:02:11.662 --> 00:02:12.641
a bit more sour.

00:02:12.641 --> 00:02:13.474
(wind whips)
- I love

00:02:13.474 --> 00:02:15.086
(bell rings)
the Cajeta Frappuccino

00:02:15.086 --> 00:02:16.148
it is very intense.

00:02:16.148 --> 00:02:18.644
- Summer, Fall and Winter.

00:02:18.644 --> 00:02:20.444
This covers your whole year.
- It does.

00:02:20.444 --> 00:02:21.694
- Which I love.

00:02:36.311 --> 00:02:39.656
(wind whipping)
(hinge squeaking)

